    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires rejecting owner creation with **400** when the email's domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com).\n\nI implemented this as a small, self-contained Bean Validation constraint \u2014 the same idiom already used in this codebase (`PostcodeValidation`, `PetAgeValidation`):\n\n1. **`DisposableEmailValidation.java`** (new) \u2014 a field-level constraint annotation.\n2. **`DisposableEmailValidator.java`** (new) \u2014 validator over `String`: extracts the domain after the last `@`, lowercases it, and rejects the three blocklisted domains. Absent/malformed emails pass through (presence/format are handled by existing field constraints).\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `x-field-extra-annotation` on the `email` property so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` carries the annotation, wiring it into the existing validation pipeline.\n\n**Structural impact:** I changed no existing functions \u2014 only added two tiny new cohesive classes (each with trivial surrounding complexity) plus one line in the OpenAPI spec. Existing methods and classes were left untouched, so `WMC_other \u00d7 CC \u00d7 changed_lines` sums to zero on modified functions.\n\nThe bad request already returns 400 via the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
